WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
mammalian BK potassium channels conduct 10 to 20 times more current than invertebrate versions, sharpening sub-milliseconds spike timing in neurons. This is Planetarian Daily, episode 220. After that, transparent cancer spheroids that split two drug readouts, social activity, and later life cognition, a teegean that ties flavor to cold hardiness, and a science deep dive on three-dimensional cell clusters. Researchers at the Okinawa Institute of Science and Technology ran molecular studies

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.780
simulations in the steps program, and mapped BK channel evolution across species.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:40.340
Each channel needs four calcium ions to open fully, and the models built that binding

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.500
step in from the start.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:46.640
Lower conductance versions force more channels to switch on to reach the same total current,

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.580
so they compete for a limited pool of free calcium.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:55.880
That contest raises variability in when a neuron fires, which the team examined in perkinji

00:00:55.880 --> 00:01:00.320
cells that need sub-millisecond precision for motor control and sensory processing.

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:05.800
Evolutionary mapping showed higher conductance tracking phylogenetic proximity to mammals.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:12.180
The study in communications biology, covered by Fizz.org, simplifies the cell to one neuron

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:12.600
type.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:18.360
Eric DeShooter noted that BK channels regulate firing across neurons, and that the models

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:21.840
offer a possible answer to why the high conductance form developed.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:27.515
Uppsala University adapted cell painting to transparent three-dimensional mini-sfears

00:01:27.515 --> 00:01:31.315
of bowel cancer cells and screened 52 oncology drugs.

00:01:31.835 --> 00:01:37.395
Two of those agents, five-flora uracil and olaperib, produced nearly identical profiles

00:01:37.395 --> 00:01:39.475
in conventional two-dimensional layers.

00:01:39.995 --> 00:01:44.875
Image cell by cell inside the spheres, they triggered distinct morphological changes,

00:01:45.415 --> 00:01:49.195
in work published in Nature Communications and reported by Fizz.org.

00:01:49.195 --> 00:01:54.195
work. The approach keeps single-cell resolution instead of averaging an entire sample into

00:01:54.195 --> 00:01:59.815
one reading. Collaboration with AstraZeneca confirmed the method transfers to other laboratories,

00:02:00.375 --> 00:02:06.526
and the team released all images, data, and code. A large international study linked participation

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:11.246
in varied and ongoing social activities to better cognitive performance in older age.

00:02:11.846 --> 00:02:17.186
The same work connected that pattern with slower age-related decline in brain health. Results

00:02:17.186 --> 00:02:22.526
disappeared online in the Journal of Epidemiology and Community Health, and Fizz.org carried

00:02:22.526 --> 00:02:23.126
the findings.

00:02:23.626 --> 00:02:27.826
The association held after the analysis accounted for other lifestyle factors.

00:02:28.406 --> 00:02:32.966
Sustained engagement across multiple activity types was the pattern tied to that protection.

00:02:33.984 --> 00:02:40.804
A team at Anhui Agricultural University identified the light-responsive gene CSBBX-19 in T-plants.

00:02:41.484 --> 00:02:46.784
The gene simultaneously adjusts the ratio of catechins to theonine in leaves, and activates

00:02:46.784 --> 00:02:52.824
a cold tolerance pathway. Investigators mapped how that single gene modulates those flavor compounds

00:02:52.824 --> 00:02:59.044
while conferring stress resistance. The work appeared in new phytologist, with fizz.org reporting the

00:02:59.044 --> 00:03:05.084
result. Corresponding author N. Huashia stated that the findings identify a valuable target for high

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:09.944
quality and high resistance tea plant breeding at higher latitudes or cooler climates.

00:03:10.889 --> 00:03:16.649
Okara, the soybean residue left after tofu and soy beverage production, was converted into a

00:03:16.649 --> 00:03:22.069
bioactive biodegradable scaffold. The material is suitable for three-dimensional printing and for

00:03:22.069 --> 00:03:27.989
skin protection or repair applications, according to Fizz.org. The work demonstrates a route to

00:03:27.989 --> 00:03:32.629
upcycle food processing waste into a functional bio material that supports tissue repair.

00:03:33.671 --> 00:03:38.591
A University of California San Diego study found that some primates increase caution toward

00:03:38.591 --> 00:03:44.491
potential germ sources after exposure to a viral threat. The shift parallels human responses

00:03:44.491 --> 00:03:48.451
observed during the COVID-19 pandemic. Fizz.org reported.

00:03:49.091 --> 00:03:52.491
The observation suggests the behavioral change is not unique to humans.

00:03:53.071 --> 00:03:56.651
It may represent a broader response to disease threats across species.

00:03:57.812 --> 00:04:01.952
Experimental evidence shows people are more likely to copy or exceed observed

00:04:01.952 --> 00:04:05.092
rule violations than to match rule following behavior.

00:04:05.692 --> 00:04:09.652
Real-world consequences can still constrain how far that copying spreads,

00:04:10.132 --> 00:04:13.952
according to Science News. The study examined how social observation

00:04:13.952 --> 00:04:16.752
influences adherence to norms and group settings.

00:04:17.708 --> 00:04:23.328
Sediment cores recovered in the 1960s from beneath a former United States military base in Greenland

00:04:23.328 --> 00:04:26.808
show the site was ice-free during an earlier warm interval.

00:04:27.468 --> 00:04:30.288
Summer temperatures then were several degrees higher than present.

00:04:30.888 --> 00:04:34.588
A university at Buffalo LED Analysis, reported by Fizz.org,

00:04:35.048 --> 00:04:37.548
provides direct evidence of those regional conditions.

00:04:38.068 --> 00:04:41.008
The cores had remained archived since the Cold War era.

00:04:41.008 --> 00:04:46.489
The University of Surrey led collection of the most extensive atmospheric data set gathered

00:04:46.489 --> 00:04:48.289
during a solar radiation event.

00:04:48.769 --> 00:04:54.209
The findings, carried by Fizz.org, underscored the need for coordinated real-time monitoring

00:04:54.209 --> 00:04:56.689
to better protect flights from radiation exposure.

00:04:57.429 --> 00:05:02.189
The work also emphasizes gaps in current aviation safety protocols during such events.

00:05:03.144 --> 00:05:08.344
A review from the University of Mississippi and Cornell University examines emerging artificial

00:05:08.344 --> 00:05:11.784
intelligence, or AI, tools for weed management.

00:05:12.164 --> 00:05:18.064
The technologies may reduce herbicide and labor needs, Fizz.org reported, yet they also

00:05:18.064 --> 00:05:21.704
introduce substantial expenses and operational challenges for growers.

00:05:22.384 --> 00:05:26.964
The analysis weighs potential reductions in chemical use against implementation barriers

00:05:26.964 --> 00:05:28.844
in real agricultural settings.

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:35.660
Experts writing in stat news suggest that vaccination messages may gain credibility by acknowledging

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:39.520
that most children recover from measles, while still stating the risks.

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:44.420
The proposal comes amid rising case counts and falling coverage in parts of the United

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:44.960
States.

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:50.220
The approach aims to address skepticism in regions where vaccination rates declined between

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:52.160
2017 and 2024.

00:05:53.209 --> 00:05:58.349
A controlled vapor process enables molecules to self-assemble into soft, quasi-crystals

00:05:58.349 --> 00:06:01.169
with uniform orientation over large areas.

00:06:01.169 --> 00:06:07.849
The method, reported by Fizz.org, addresses a key fabrication obstacle for these non-periodic

00:06:07.849 --> 00:06:08.609
ordered materials.

00:06:09.169 --> 00:06:14.209
It overcomes previous difficulties in achieving consistent alignment across extended surfaces.

00:06:15.399 --> 00:06:20.459
Volunteer researchers also today documented saltwater intrusion and erosion, threatening

00:06:20.459 --> 00:06:26.079
the freshwater Horseshoe Bay Lagoon and its bull-caroo sedge habitat on magnetic island, with

00:06:26.079 --> 00:06:27.899
major repairs needed to save it.

00:06:27.899 --> 00:06:33.039
Something most people get wrong is the idea that a flat layer of cancer cells on plastic

00:06:33.039 --> 00:06:36.699
is a faithful preview of how a drug will act inside living tissue.

00:06:37.399 --> 00:06:42.179
Cells in the body sit in three-dimensional clusters, where neighbors, nutrient gradients

00:06:42.179 --> 00:06:45.279
and mechanical forces differ sharply from those on a dish.

00:06:45.819 --> 00:06:50.919
The minisfears were made optically clear with a sugar and glycerol solution, so individual

00:06:50.919 --> 00:06:54.459
cells deep inside each cluster stayed visible under the microscope.

00:06:54.459 --> 00:07:00.299
That clearing step let the team apply cell painting, which labels nuclei, mitochondria,

00:07:00.539 --> 00:07:06.301
and internal scaffolding across thousands of cells per sphere. Microscopes then captured

00:07:06.301 --> 00:07:10.261
thousands of shape and structure measurements from cells that would otherwise have been

00:07:10.261 --> 00:07:11.061
hidden in the core.

00:07:11.661 --> 00:07:16.801
Follow-up gene expression data pointed to stronger activation of the P53 stress response

00:07:16.801 --> 00:07:22.671
pathway by five-flora uracil, even though it produced less detectable DNA damage than

00:07:22.671 --> 00:07:27.891
olaperib. That split in pathway engagement was invisible when the same agents were scored

00:07:27.891 --> 00:07:33.311
on a flat layer. Preserving spatial context therefore changes which cellular features a compound

00:07:33.311 --> 00:07:38.671
appears to alter. The workflow runs in standard plates, so other groups can now test whether

00:07:38.671 --> 00:07:44.351
additional drug pairs separate once cells are read one by one inside a cluster. Every image,

00:07:44.671 --> 00:07:49.451
measurement, and analysis script has been released so the comparisons can be repeated or extended.

00:07:49.451 --> 00:07:54.171
screening pipelines that still rely on two-dimensional readouts may advance or

00:07:54.171 --> 00:07:59.160
discard compounds on incomplete cellular information. Before we go, the

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:03.800
transparent spheroid workflow is being extended to patient-derived organoids to

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:07.560
test whether the same hidden drug distinctions appear in more complex tissue

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:12.620
models. That's Planetarian Daily for today. If you enjoyed this, a rating or

